# YouTube Playlist Downloader — core

- Tauri v2 desktop app: React 19 + TS + Vite + Tailwind 4 + Zustand / Rust backend
- GPL-3.0 app license; official builds also ship **LGPL FFmpeg/ffprobe** sidecars (see `docs/THIRD_PARTY.md`). No telemetry/accounts; personal offline use framing
- Settings in `settings.json` (plugin-store): folder, concurrency 1–8 (default 3), `m4a`|`mp3`, `locale` `ko`|`en`
- Official releases: **Apple Silicon Mac + Windows x64**. **Intel Mac and Linux official binaries: not planned** (build from source). **Apple Notarization: not planned** (Gatekeeper docs only).
- yt-dlp is bundled as sidecar; in-app update writes **app-data override** under `sidecars/` (does not rewrite the release bundle)
- FFmpeg/ffprobe are bundled LGPL sidecars (`scripts/prepare-ffmpeg-sidecar.sh`); runtime prefers bundled, then system PATH. Deno stays optional/system-only
- Prefer Korean communication with the maintainer; keep changes focused (no drive-by refactors)

## Entry points

| Task | Where |
| :--- | :--- |
| Download UX | `src/hooks/useDownloadActions.ts`, `src/store/downloadStore.ts` |
| yt-dlp / progress / skip probe | `src-tauri/src/services/ytdlp.rs`, `ytdlp_update.rs` |
| yt-dlp update UI | `src/components/Header.tsx` (override via `ytdlp_update.rs`) |
| Env diagnose | `src-tauri/src/services/environment.rs`, `src/components/Footer.tsx` |
| FFmpeg sidecar prep | `scripts/prepare-ffmpeg-sidecar.sh`, `docs/RELEASING.md` |
| i18n | `src/i18n/` (`ko.ts` + `en.ts` always both) |
| Release | `.github/workflows/release.yml`, `docs/RELEASING.md` |

